  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The accessibility of the chatbox from the radial menu is a bit obtuse, and difficult to find. Especially considering it's listed under \"Options\". \nAs an alternative, I think a dedicated button should be placed near or around the microphone mute/unmute button in the quickmenu. It's placement would make accessing the chatbox a very swift action that can be preformed in VR and desktop easier, similar to how muting and unmuting already is. The radial menus in general can be very important for puppeteering avatars. More often than not, requiring both hands to be occupied with specific submenus. They're very short on real-estate. Menu hunting through them to return to the chatbox can become very cumbersome. Ideally, the options submenu should probably be accessed very rarely.\n \nAlternatively, a 4th radial menu slot for \"Tools\" could be added to the radial menu, where personal mirror and chatbox can exist independent of the options submenu.",
